From abbe08a9dba678afeb4f5f8d33754575e54a1ff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:54:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Campaign wave 8: the epilogue's kitchen, the tap turned
 by his own hand

After the dinner the player has the kitchen: Arthur goes to the sink to listen to
the pipe, Twinsen turns the tap's handle himself (his hand on its knob), the water
runs cold into Arthur's cup under the spout and the wall stays quiet; Arthur keeps
the cup there just in case. Then a word with Zoe, and the end screen.

New flags only (ep_v ep_tap ep_word). A save from before at the epilogue's start
plays the dinner again (it loaded into a quiet house before); one past the dinner
counts the step as done. The tap's handle sits on a short stem at the end of the
pipe's run (the spout has not moved) so his hand reaches it. Fixtures base-16*
(made on the build before) and new-16-kitchen, new-16-tap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012GFEakZyL3XxjZKHRj5dFg
